.TH MOD_TILE 5 "2026-10-25" "mod_tile v0.8.1"
.\" Please adjust this date whenever revising the manpage.
.SH NAME
mod_tile \- Apache HTTPD module for serving tiles and communicating with renderd
.SH SYNOPSIS
Apache HTTP server configuration directives for \fBmod_tile\fR.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmod_tile\fR is an Apache module that serves map tiles created by rendering pipelines. It communicates with the rendering daemon (\fBrenderd\fR) over UNIX or TCP sockets to request tiles on demand and manages on-disk caching, throttling, and stale tile management.
.SH DIRECTIVES
.SS Core Layer Configuration & Loading
.TP
.BI AddTileConfig " url_path renderd_config_name " [ key=value\ ... ]
Configures a tile layer mapping by defining a URL path, target renderd.conf map section, and optional key-value settings.
.RS
.PP
.B Supported Key-Value Options:
.TP
.BI minzoom= integer
Minimum zoom level for this layer. Must be non-negative (\fBminzoom >= 0\fP). [Default: \fB0\fP]
.TP
.BI maxzoom= integer
Maximum zoom level for this layer. Must not exceed \fB30\fP (\fBMAX_ZOOM_SERVER\fP). [Default: \fB20\fP (\fBMAX_ZOOM\fP)]
.TP
.BI extension= string
File extension for served tiles. [Default: \fBpng\fP]
.TP
.BI mimetype= string
MIME content type header returned for tile responses. [Default: \fBimage/png\fP]
.TP
.BI tile_dir= path
Custom storage directory path for this layer's tile cache. [Default: empty string, falls back to global \fBModTileTileDir\fP]
.PP
.B Validation:
An error is returned if \fBminzoom < 0\fP or \fBmaxzoom > 30\fP (\fBMAX_ZOOM_SERVER\fP).
.RE
.TP
.BI AddTileMimeConfig " url_path renderd_config_name file_extension"
Legacy directive to configure tile layer mapping with explicit file extension handling.
.RS
.PP
.B Zoom Defaults:
Defaults \fBminzoom\fP to \fB0\fP and \fBmaxzoom\fP to \fB20\fP (\fBMAX_ZOOM\fP).
.RE
.TP
.BI LoadTileConfigFile " config_file_name"
Loads an entire \fBrenderd.conf\fP configuration file into Apache.
.RS
.PP
.B Capacity Limit:
Processes up to \fB100\fP map sections (\fBXMLCONFIGS_MAX\fP).
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileTileDir " directory_path"
Sets the global default file system directory where cached rendered tiles are stored on disk.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fI/var/cache/renderd/tiles\fP (\fBRENDERD_TILE_DIR\fP)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileBulkMode " On|Off"
Enables bulk rendering mode for requests sent to \fBrenderd\fP.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fBOff\fP (\fB0\fP)
.PP
.B Description:
Forces all requests sent to \fBrenderd\fP to run with bulk rendering priority and prevents tiles from being marked dirty.
.RE
.SS Caching & Expiration Control
.TP
.BI ModTileCacheDurationMinimum " seconds"
Sets the baseline minimum cache expiry duration for served tiles.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fB10800\fP seconds (3 hours)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileCacheDurationMax " seconds"
Sets the absolute maximum cache expiry duration for served tiles.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fB604800\fP seconds (7 days)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileCacheDurationDirty " seconds"
Sets the cache expiry duration applied when serving dirty (stale) tiles.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fB900\fP seconds (15 minutes)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileCacheDurationLowZoom " zoom_level duration_seconds"
Sets the cache threshold level and duration for low zoom tiles.
.RS
.PP
.B Default Duration:
\fB518400\fP seconds (6 days)
.PP
.B Default Level:
\fB0\fP
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileCacheDurationMediumZoom " zoom_level duration_seconds"
Sets the cache threshold level and duration for medium zoom tiles.
.RS
.PP
.B Default Duration:
\fB86400\fP seconds (24 hours)
.PP
.B Default Level:
\fB0\fP
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileCacheLastModifiedFactor " factor"
Sets the multiplier factor by which the last-modified timestamp determines dynamic cache expiration. Accepts a float.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fB0.0\fP
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileVeryOldThreshold " microseconds"
Sets the age threshold (in microseconds) beyond which an outdated tile is considered "very old" and rendered with elevated priority.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fB31536000000000\fP microseconds (365 days) (\fBVERYOLD_THRESHOLD\fP)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileCacheExtendedDuration " seconds"
Sets the length of time for extended period caching.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fB0\fP
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileCacheExtendedHostName " hostname"
Sets the hostname used for extended period caching requests.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
Empty string (\fI""\fP)
.RE
.SS Daemon & Server Communication
.TP
.BI ModTileRenderdSocketName " socket_path"
Sets the path to the Unix domain socket used to communicate with the rendering daemon (\fBrenderd\fP).
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fI/run/renderd/renderd.sock\fP (\fBRENDERD_SOCKET\fP)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileRenderdSocketAddr " host_or_ip port"
Configures a TCP socket host address and port for connecting to \fBrenderd\fP.
.RS
.PP
.B Default Port:
\fB0\fP (disabled, defaults to Unix domain socket)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileRequestTimeout " seconds"
Sets the timeout limit in seconds on standard tile requests to renderd.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fB3\fP seconds (\fBREQUEST_TIMEOUT\fP)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileMissingRequestTimeout " seconds"
Sets the timeout limit in seconds on priority rendering requests for missing tiles.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fB3\fP seconds (\fBREQUEST_TIMEOUT\fP)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileMaxLoadMissing " system_load"
Sets the maximum system load average threshold above which missing tiles will not be rendered on demand.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fB50\fP (\fBMAX_LOAD_MISSING\fP)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileMaxLoadOld " system_load"
Sets the maximum system load average threshold above which outdated tiles will not be re-rendered.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fB16\fP (\fBMAX_LOAD_OLD\fP)
.RE
.SS Endpoint Options
.TP
.BI ModTileEnableDirtyURL " On|Off"
Enables or disables handling of \fI.../dirty\fP requests to manually force tile re-rendering.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fBOn\fP (\fB1\fP)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileEnableStatusURL " On|Off"
Enables or disables handling of \fI.../status\fP monitoring endpoints.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fBOn\fP (\fB1\fP)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileEnableStats " On|Off"
Enables or disables keeping global statistics about tile serving metrics.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fBOn\fP (\fB1\fP)
.RE
.SS Throttling & Rate Limiting
.TP
.BI ModTileEnableTileThrottling " On|Off"
Enables or disables IP-based rate limiting for tile downloads.
.RS
.PP
.B Default:
\fBOff\fP (\fB0\fP)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileEnableTileThrottlingXForward " mode"
Controls extraction of client IP from \fBX-Forwarded-For\fP header for rate limiting.
.RS
.PP
.B Values:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0\fP: Off (Default). Uses direct client connection IP.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB1\fP: Use the first entry (originating client IP).
.IP \(bu 2
\fB2\fP: Use the last entry in the proxy chain.
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileThrottlingTiles " bucket_size top_up_rate"
Configures token bucket capacity (integer tile count) and top-up rate (microseconds) for total tile downloads per IP.
.RS
.PP
.B Defaults:
Bucket size: \fB5000\fP (\fBAVAILABLE_TILE_BUCKET_SIZE\fP), Top-up rate: \fB1000000\fP \(mus (\fBTILE_TOPUP_RATE\fP)
.RE
.TP
.BI ModTileThrottlingRenders " bucket_size top_up_rate"
Configures token bucket capacity (integer render count) and top-up rate (microseconds) for rendering requests per IP.
.RS
.PP
.B Defaults:
Bucket size: \fB65\fP (\fBAVAILABLE_RENDER_BUCKET_SIZE\fP), Top-up rate: \fB5000000\fP \(mus (\fBRENDER_TOPUP_RATE\fP)
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR renderd(1),
.BR renderd.conf(5)
.SH AUTHOR
mod_tile was written by Jon Burgess, and other OpenStreetMap project members.
.PP
